<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 792 0 R
/E (The top module instantiates the DUT \(Design Under Test\) and the physical Interface. Additionally, the top module uses the bind construct to connect the  assertions module to the DUT to continuously monitor and verify the hardware behavior.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
176 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 793 0 R
/E (UVM Test & Sequences: The top module calls run_test\(\), which dynamically creates the test component using the UVM factory and starts the UVM phases. Inside the test, the environment is built, and based on the verification plan, three main sequences are generated and executed on the sequencer: a write_only_sequence, a read_only_sequence, and a concurrent write_read_sequence)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
177 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 794 0 R
/E (Driving the Interface: The driver pulls these transactions from the sequencer and translates them into pin-level signals. It drives these signals onto the physical Interface via its virtual interface handle. )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
178 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 795 0 R
/E (Monitoring: The monitor continuously observes the pin-level activity on the Interface \(also via a virtual interface\). It converts these physical signals back into transaction-level objects. )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
